{
  "name": "gecko",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/gecko.py): the MOORISH GECKO, Tarentola mauritanica, 15 cm, the tail half of it. A BIG FLAT TRIANGULAR HEAD, wide at the jowls, on a distinct neck; HUGE LIDLESS EYES under their clear spectacle, the pupil a vertical slit; a flat broad trunk sprawled low, the elbows and knees held high, the back studded with rows of TUBERCLES (`osteoderms`); short splayed toes each ending in a BROAD ADHESIVE PAD (a flat spatula, pale lamellae beneath); a PLUMP tail, thick and soft nearly to its end, ringed with tubercles. Sandy grey with broad dark crossbands over the back and rings on the tail, pale tubercles. Coats: Moorish, Tokay (Gekko gecko: blue-grey with orange spots, x2), Mediterranean house gecko (pale pinkish, .7).",
